[Lecture6.pdf p.4] Code Review 
Don’t overuse this-> 
No need for this->_member, just write _member 
(that’s why we use a leading underscore - to distinguish member 
variables) 
Much better: 
void Rational::normalize() { 
auto abs_num = std::abs( _num ); 
auto abs_den = std::abs( _den ); 
auto theSign = sign(); 
// ..etc, ^^^ better 
} 
Andre Kessler 
